module gunbc.primitive_egress_census_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust that realizes the two compiler queries the primitive
// egress census (gunbc.primitive_egress.census_live, gunbc#11642) consumes. Same shape and same
// owner as gunbc.evaluation_store_address_census_seed_growth, whose builtins are this change's
// precedent: a .dag-only re-derivation of the resolver's callee identity or of the compiled
// registry's key set would be a SECOND resolver beside the compiler (DESIGN section 3), so the
// instruments ask the seed and the seed answers with its own product.
//
// PURPOSE (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing). PRIMITIVE-EGRESS-0 (gunbc#11626)
// needs one derived denominator whose deciding consumer edge is resolver-produced callee identity
// -- CallTargetIdentity::RuntimePrimitiveCall and MethodSemantics::AlgebraMethodSemantics on the
// typed tree -- never a text search. compile_dag_primitive_call_edges walks every entry of a pool
// through a PRIVATE index and projects exactly those sites (plus the sites where the resolver
// established nothing, carried as typed unresolved rows). builtin_function_registry_keys reads the
// compiled registry's key set because its values carry Node and the interpreter cannot evaluate
// the data row (NoSuchField Node.ident), which is why std.primitives has carried a hand roster
// that this census now measures against the authority instead of inheriting.
//
// WHAT IS NOT NETTED. Generated dispatch rows in v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated.rs are
// projections of gunbc.v1.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface and exempt by generation authority;
// BuiltinSignature inserts in v1_compiler_infer_method extend an existing map
// (ExistingSeedItemModified). The census classifies BOTH builtins as CompilerQueryFrontier rows in
// its own denominator (gunbc.primitive_egress.dispositions_seed_query), so the instrument does not
// exempt itself from the join it performs.
data primitive_egress_census_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "PrimitiveCalleeIdentity", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "PrimitiveCallEdgeRow", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "PrimitiveCallEntryRefusal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "PrimitiveCallEdgeCensus", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "builtin_function_registry_keys", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "primitive_call_callee_of_target", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "collect_primitive_call_edges", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "primitive_call_edge_at", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "compile_dag_primitive_call_edges_on_this_thread", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "primitive_call_edges_from_module", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.emit_host", decl_name: "compile_dag_primitive_call_edges", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "primitive_callee_identity_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "primitive_call_edge_census_value", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "The primitive egress census asks the compiler which call sites it resolved to a runtime primitive, an algebra method template, a service operation, or nothing, and asks the compiled registry for its key set. Both are seed pipeline products with no substrate representation a .dag fold could read: the typed tree's CallTargetIdentity lives in the resolver's output and the registry's values carry Node. compile_dag_primitive_call_edges takes the primary-root closure of each pool root through a private MultiEntryIndex, resolves the union ONCE under the compile-clean admission (the route gunbc compile takes for a primary root), and walks every module of that one graph whose path starts with a requested entry prefix (all when none are given); a module with a blocking diagnostic is a typed refusal row, refuses nothing silently (a blocking entry is a typed refusal row the consumer must decide on), walks each entry's own module once, and projects the callee identity with the caller's declaration identity and span. builtin_function_registry_keys returns the sorted key set. The two v1_interpreter projections lift the carriers into interpreter values. The enrolled instrument is gunbc.primitive_egress.census_live primitive_egress_census_exit, reached as gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:primitive-egress-census.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these items when option A lands: the floor exposes its accepted live-tree resolution product (or an equivalent exact query interface) and the census derives primitive callee identity over the complete production roots without building another corpus index per run -- the same capability gunbc.evaluation_store_address_census_seed_growth names. The registry key query dissolves when builtin_function_registry is constructed FROM a .dag roster the interpreter can evaluate (std.primitives builtin_registry_surface_names_note names that fold), at which point the hand roster and this query are one list.",
  current_boundary: "Reachable only as .dag free-calls. The edge query reads the pool roots it is given, resolves through a private index, never occupies the process-shared slot, writes nothing, and substitutes no value for a refused entry. The key query reads the compiled map and nothing else."
}
